      "writtenOn": "2025-01-17T20:12:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is also the reverse race - if the other thread\u0027s raise to y comes first then A may read y as the old priority and hence restore that rather than x afterwards. Whether that is a problem or not depends on how the other thread operates, but given #3 and #4 below I understand it\u0027s not expected that it will ever try to restore an earlier priority if the app has had an opportunity to do its own restore.\n\nGiven that, to avoid this reverse race it\u0027s important that the app reads the cached priority as x, presumably through `Thread.getPriority`. That seems worth mentioning in #1 below.",
