      "writtenOn": "2025-01-17T20:12:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t have a precise meaning to me - make it more explicit?\n\nOr else, iiuc the gist here is that an external process really can\u0027t make any assumptions that a priority it sets will remain set for any amount of time. Presumably in a situation like that there would be some sort understanding between the app and the external process so they don\u0027t fight each other, but ART can still always come in and change the priority and then restore it to the cached one.\n\nIf that understanding is correct then I\u0027d express it something like this instead: External processes should avoid updating priorities of threads executing managed code (and hence enters ART). If they do, ART can at any moment overwrite their updates and restore the cached priority.",
